{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399691-shalim","id":1399691,"title":"Shalim","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-28T16:35:56-07:00","id":1399691,"title":"Shalim","content":"So... in Chicago by Night there's the descriprion of this character, Rabbi Michalis Basaras. He's a childer of Giangaleazzo of Milan who apparently met a shadow creature calling itself &quot;the Traveller&quot; (it also has another name given in Cults of the Blood Gods) who told him of &quot;Shalim&quot; claiming it was the progenitor of all Lasombras and meant to bring everything into the Abyss. Michalis joined the cult of Shalim and is working to bring oblivion to reality. The passage also mentions that Giangaleazzo may have been part of some conspiracy of sorts and he was just waiting to betray the Sabbat until something triggered the event.<br /> <br /> So here's my questions:<br /> <br /> -Who or what do we think &quot;the Traveller&quot; really is?<br /> -Could &quot;Shalim&quot; really be Lasombra itself after spending a few centuries into the Abyss?<br /> -What is Giangaleazzo exactly up to in your opinion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T16:48:17-07:00","id":1399697,"title":"","content":"1. I definitely believe that Shalim is &quot;just&quot; the Lasombra Antediluvian but that said Antediluvian has adopted a kind of Nephandus-esque, &quot;I will unmake reality and plunge it into eternal night&quot; kind of attitude.<br /> <br /> 2. I believe that Gangalezzo is probably using the cult versus being a member of it. He's already betrayed one fanatical group of Gehenna cultists.<br /> <br /> 3. Just for fun, I believe the Traveller is Moncada.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T00:58:11-07:00","id":1399751,"title":"","content":"The Traveller is [Lasombra]. Shalim is fiction meant to organize cults.<br /> This would fit the Lasombra archetype of being power behind the throne better than [Lasombra] being Shalim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T06:35:09-07:00","id":1399806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399691-shalim?p=1399697#post1399697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I definitely believe that Shalim is &quot;just&quot; the Lasombra Antediluvian but that said Antediluvian has adopted a kind of Nephandus-esque, &quot;I will unmake reality and plunge it into eternal night&quot; kind of attitude.<br /> <br /> 2. I believe that Gangalezzo is probably using the cult versus being a member of it. He's already betrayed one fanatical group of Gehenna cultists.<br /> <br /> 3. Just for fun, I believe the Traveller is Moncada.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. If Shalim is Lasombra it might not be aware he's been given that name. It being up to no good was always the case though (previously it meant to plunge the world into eternal darkness, basically the same thing as unleashing Oblivion.<br /> <br /> 2. Nowhere it's stated Giangaleazzo is working with the cult. He just receives some undiscolsed information, sets the plan to betray the Sabbat in motion and sends Michalis away from Milan (to protect him?), refusing to make contact with him afterwards. It is then that Michalis meets the Traveller and learns of &quot;Shalim&quot;. Giangaleazzo's actions were the prototype for the later mass defection of the Lasombra's from the Sabbat. Personally I'm inclined to think Giangaleazzo was in cahoots with Montano.<br /> <br /> 3. Seems unlikely, Moncanda was probably still undead when the Traveller visited Michalis, but it might make an interesting twist for a story involving Lucita.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399691-shalim?p=1399751#post1399751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Traveller is [Lasombra]. Shalim is fiction meant to organize cults.<br /> This would fit the Lasombra archetype of being power behind the throne better than [Lasombra] being Shalim.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting take. The Lasombra archetype is more like &quot;I don't care about the trappings of power as long I am the one in power&quot; while for the Ventrue it's important to be seen as the ones in charge, though. A small but significant difference. That said if Lasombra is free from the Abyss it could very well be orchestrating this whole thing, or it could just be a demon/spectre/wyrm creature.<br /> <br /> Personally I believe the emergence of &quot;Shalim&quot; and possibly &quot;the Traveller&quot; itself match the last chapter of BJD. Right in the end we have something emerge from the Abyss portal of Castel d'Ombro. The Traveller could be an ancient childer of Lasombra himself or at least a 5th generation vampire (Zarathustra?). Certainly I find it curious one of the in character tales included in CbN regarding the Lasombras mentions one of the defectors fleeing the Middle East and the Sabbat after a disastrous encounter with something that fits the description of the creature that was awakened at the end of BJD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 06-30-2020, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T08:12:59-07:00","id":1399830,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that Moncada becomes a horrific abyssal THING post-death in the Gehenna novel and kills Lucita. It's a mutual kill, though, and how she achieves a bit of redemption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T08:30:23-07:00","id":1399836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399691-shalim?p=1399830#post1399830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be noted that Moncada becomes a horrific abyssal THING post-death in the Gehenna novel and kills Lucita. It's a mutual kill, though, and how she achieves a bit of redemption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Moncanda summoned such creature in the Lasombra Trilogy when Lucita and Fatima were at last able to kill him. Then in Gehenna SOMETHING with Moncanda's memories attacked and killed Lucita, IIRC the creature did so with Kapaneus present. I always took the creature for the returned Lasombra antediluvian who somehow had the memories of several practitioners of shadow summoning magic, including Moncanda.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T08:36:10-07:00","id":1399839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399691-shalim?p=1399836#post1399836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Moncanda summoned such creature in the Lasombra Trilogy when Lucita and Fatima were at last able to kill him. Then in Gehenna SOMETHING with Moncanda's memories attacked and killed Lucita, IIRC the creature did so with Kapaneus present. I always took the creature for the returned Lasombra antediluvian who somehow had the memories of several practitioners of shadow summoning magic, including Moncanda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. My take was that it was the fact that the Path of Night transformed its Kindred (even post-mortem) into Shadow Demons ala Warhammer 40K and Chaos. Moncada was &quot;rewarded&quot; by becoming something beyond human.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T04:40:26-07:00","id":1400046,"title":"","content":"I never really liked the idea that Lasombra was totally successful in its plans when Gratiano tried to do a coup. If an Antediluvian achieves its Jyhad goal, or at least what must be a major aim, I feel there should be some kind of notable repercussions. Unless its only goal was to drop out of the public eye with a cover story, and the whole resto of it was of little concern. (For an Antediluvian, it had been extremely visible for a very long time. And with a know location. Very different from the modus operandi of the rest of the clan. It may have gotten antsy about its visibility after the diablerie of Saulot.)<br /> <br /> But if it really tried to merge with the Abyss or something, I feel there must have been a fuckup somewhere. Similar to Cappadocious &quot;eat God&quot; plan.<br /> <br /> So there might be some sort of Abyss shadow of Lasombra still extant, like the wraith of Cappadocious.<br /> <br /> It does fit the notion that Gehenna approaches, and some Antediluvians take the chance of trying to make their final moves before their plans are quite perfected. To get there before their rivals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2471,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","user":"Trollroot","date":". 06-30-2020, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T05:46:52-07:00","id":1400056,"title":"","content":"Question about the Abyss<br /> <br /> Is it the same as the Abyss in Werewolf? Or is it more like the Abyss the Qlippoth grows out of in Mage Book of the Fallen?<br /> <br /> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> that Shalim is Lasombra but transformed by their time in the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T05:47:55-07:00","id":1400058,"title":"","content":"Sorry. I like figuring out how stuff ties together (cosmology?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T06:16:57-07:00","id":1400076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399691-shalim?p=1400056#post1400056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about the Abyss<br /> <br /> Is it the same as the Abyss in Werewolf? Or is it more like the Abyss the Qlippoth grows out of in Mage Book of the Fallen?<br /> <br /> I agree with <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> that Shalim is Lasombra but transformed by their time in the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>The short answer: no one is sure.<br /> <br /> Slightly longer answer: in the WoD there are several \u201clocations\u201d fitting the description of what the Abyss is. The place where the neverborn rest? The prison of the demons? Some wyrm realm? The answer depends in the game you want to play. That said, V5 is apparently referring to the Abyss as the Wraith: the Oblivion version of the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T06:17:43-07:00","id":1400078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399691-shalim?p=1400056#post1400056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about the Abyss<br /> <br /> Is it the same as the Abyss in Werewolf? Or is it more like the Abyss the Qlippoth grows out of in Mage Book of the Fallen?<br /> <br /> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> that Shalim is Lasombra but transformed by their time in the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of people were somewhat upset that Demon: The Fallen linked the Abyss, the Labyrinth, and the Underworld all together into one single thing.<br /> <br /> So Oblivion as a combo of Obternation and Necromancy actually makes a certain amount of sense.<br /> <br /> It's just plenty of people never actually accepted or heard that retcon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T06:19:18-07:00","id":1400079,"title":"","content":"Shalim:<ul><li>Grandmother from <i>Orpheus</i>. She would be the most important figure in Oblivion if she exists, but I'm not sure if the origins match up or how she'd be connected to Kindred</li> <li>An unknown progenitor of kindred, including Caine, whose actions are attributed to God in Noddist myth. This barely answers question, but I like it anyway.</li> <li>The Lasombra antideluvian. I suppose if a kindred can master the void of universe, this could work, but I'd prefer something more primordial.</li> </ul><br /> Apolleon the Traveler: He's actually called an &quot;ancient Lasombra&quot; in <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i>, which narrows it down. Lasombra himself is unlikely to be called a Lasombra, but it's possible. He spends most of his time on the seabed, so he probably isn't well known. I'd rather see Zarathustra being his best self in Antioch.<br /> <br /> Giangaleazzo: Nothing to do with Shalim I imagine, but I should think that he's interested in his clanmates joining him in the Camarilla, whether he likes it or not. If nothing else, it could draw vengeful attention from the Sabbat away from him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399691-shalim?p=1400056#post1400056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about the Abyss<br /> <br /> Is it the same as the Abyss in Werewolf? Or is it more like the Abyss the Qlippoth grows out of in Mage Book of the Fallen?<br /> <br /> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> that Shalim is Lasombra but transformed by their time in the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't really have a consensus on that. It was discussed in a fairly recent <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1392809-v5-did-the-lasombra-right-and-wrong/page18\">thread</a> about Lasombra. I said what I think it is in post 268.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T08:02:30-07:00","id":1400089,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys. My personal opinion is that the Abyss that Oblivion draws its power from is located in the Underworld and is the same place as the Qlippothic Abyss in Book of the Fallen and the prison of the Fallen from D:tF. It is NOT the same as the Abyss in Werewolf, which is located in the Middle Umbra. But that\u2019s just me (and my ST, who I just talked about this with).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T15:52:04-07:00","id":1400196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399691-shalim?p=1400089#post1400089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks guys. My personal opinion is that the Abyss that Oblivion draws its power from is located in the Underworld and is the same place as the Qlippothic Abyss in Book of the Fallen and the prison of the Fallen from D:tF. It is NOT the same as the Abyss in Werewolf, which is located in the Middle Umbra. But that\u2019s just me (and my ST, who I just talked about this with).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly a &quot;rational&quot; way to look at the question. Side note: keep in mind the discipline of oblivion shares its name with Oblivion, the power of anticreation that resides below the Labyrinth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T16:13:07-07:00","id":1400201,"title":"","content":"I know!!!<br /> <br /> That\u2019s one reason we decided to make the two Abysses the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T17:50:36-07:00","id":1400433,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that it's not a literal place but rather the very thing behind the concept of dissolution and nonexistence, which affects all realms in some way. The caveat is that in the various spirit worlds concepts can be like places, so the &quot;lower&quot; edges of all the umbral realms, the underworld, etc., end up being frayed and distorted by proximity to this principle of nothingness, and sentient beings that spend time in proximity to it can end up maddened servants of non-being that work towards bringing about the end of all things.<br /> <br /> It's not hard to see how an ancient of the Lasombra bloodline could end up identifying with this nothingness and be utterly corrupted by it. The eldest, if they still exist in any meaningful sense, would be a good candidate, but there are certainly others...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T18:31:55-07:00","id":1400441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399691-shalim?p=1400433#post1400433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that it's not a literal place but rather the very thing behind the concept of dissolution and nonexistence, which affects all realms in some way. The caveat is that in the various spirit worlds concepts can be like places, so the &amp;quot;lower&amp;quot; edges of all the umbral realms, the underworld, etc., end up being frayed and distorted by proximity to this principle of nothingness, and sentient beings that spend time in proximity to it can end up maddened servants of non-being that work towards bringing about the end of all things.<br /> <br /> It's not hard to see how an ancient of the Lasombra bloodline could end up identifying with this nothingness and be utterly corrupted by it. The eldest, if they still exist in any meaningful sense, would be a good candidate, but there are certainly others...</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer a more literal interpretation, but thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}